From: Batman <batman@Batman.local>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 18:56:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] browse patch 012: noise canvas toDataURL()/toBlob() readback
 per origin
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

toDataURL() and toBlob() are the other two classic canvas-
fingerprinting readouts alongside getImageData() (patch 011): draw a
deterministic scene, export it (as a data: URL or Blob), hash the
bytes.

Extracts the noise algorithm from patch 011 into a shared
third_party/blink/renderer/platform/graphics/canvas_noise.{h,cc} —
one place to review the actual perturbation logic, used from both
BaseRenderingContext2D::getImageDataInternal (canvas2d, unchanged
behavior) and the two new call sites below.

Both toDataURL() (HTMLCanvasElement::ToDataURLInternal, via
ImageDataBuffer::Create) and toBlob() (CanvasAsyncBlobCreator's
constructor, which also backs OffscreenCanvas.convertToBlob()) reach
their pixels through SkImage::peekPixels() — a zero-copy view into
memory the image still owns, potentially shared with the canvas's own
compositing output. Mutating that in place would corrupt whatever
else references it, unlike getImageData()'s always-fresh ImageData
buffer. The new shared helper
MakePrivateCanvasSnapshotAndApplyNoise() makes an exclusively-owned
copy via SkImage::readPixels() first — the same technique
ImageDataBuffer's own constructor already uses for its
texture-backed branch — then applies the noise to that copy.

ImageDataBuffer::ApplyOriginNoise() is scoped deliberately: only the
two canvas call sites invoke it. ImageDataBuffer::Create is also used
by DevTools audits, accessibility, and video poster capture, none of
which are JS-exposed fingerprinting surfaces — noising those would be
pointless and risks visible corruption of unrelated browser features
that happen to reuse the same utility class.
